  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1979-p19.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(256=2^8,\\) \\[ 256^{32}=2^{256}. \\] Thus \\((\\frac{x}{2})^{256}=1.\\) The real solutions are \\(x=2\\) and \\(x=-2,\\) and the sum of their squares is \\(4+4=8.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite \\(256^{32}\\) as a single power with exponent \\(256\\)",
        "Determine the two real values whose \\(256\\)th powers equal \\(2^{256}\\)"
      ],
